{% from 'networkpolicy.yml.j2' import networkpolicy with context %}
---
# The baseline (k8s/roles/netpol-baseline) admits traefik, prometheus and the node bridges to
# every pod carrying `netpol-baseline: enforced`. This file adds sonarr's own callers, which are
# all direct pod → ClusterIP and therefore invisible to the baseline.
#
# This rule is PORT-SCOPED: the baseline admits none of janitorr, configarr, monitor-bridge,
# autofix-bridge, bazarr, prowlarr, sonarr-verify, janitorr-verify or homepage, so they reach
# sonarr only through this rule and only on this one port.
#
# TRAEFIK IS LISTED DELIBERATELY — do not remove it as redundant. While sonarr carries the
# baseline label the union is the same with or without it. The entry matters for a pod that
# lacks the label, which this policy alone selects, and it keeps this policy's caller set
# complete if the baseline's traefik rule is ever port-scoped.
#
# bazarr addresses sonarr by BARE NAME from its own application database (see
# k8s/roles/bazarr/defaults/main.yml), so no grep finds it; dropping it breaks subtitle fetching
# silently.
#
# prowlarr is here for the REVERSE direction: its Application Sync POSTs indexer definitions INTO
# sonarr over the ClusterIP, configured in prowlarr's own database. Fenced, sonarr silently keeps
# stale indexer definitions and nothing alerts, because monitor-bridge's "Prowlarr Indexers" check
# reads prowlarr's own /api/v1/indexerstatus.
#
# homepage's widget reads /api/v3/queue over the ClusterIP, not through Traefik, because sonarr's
# public route is Authelia-gated and its monitoring IngressRoute exposes only one path; fencing it
# out breaks the widget.
#
# sonarr-verify is the pod label of the Jobs in templates/verify/; without this entry the fence
# refuses their API calls.
# janitorr-verify is janitorr's verify Job label. No pod carries it until janitorr's Flux flip,
# and tests/k8s/edge/test_netpol_from.py holds it in STAGED_CALLERS until then.
#
# The caller list is `netpol_from:` on this role's containers_list entry (cluster/services.yml),
# each caller's reason beside it. `homepage_widget: true` adds homepage through the
# `netpol_callers` filter, and `netpol_role_owned: true` keeps netpol-baseline from
# rendering a second copy.
{{ networkpolicy(container_item.name, container_item.port, container_item | netpol_callers) }}
